# VASP: vibrational frequencies of the adsorbed molecule (finite displacements)
# Run AFTER INCAR.relax on the optimised mol@slab. Freeze Au, displace only the
# molecule's atoms (via POTIM sign + selective dynamics) for an affordable Hessian.
SYSTEM = adsorbed-molecule frequencies

PREC   = Accurate
ENCUT  = 400
EDIFF  = 1E-7        # tight — frequencies need accurate forces
IBRION = 5           # finite-difference Hessian
NFREE  = 2
POTIM  = 0.015       # displacement (Å)
ISMEAR = 1
SIGMA  = 0.1
GGA    = PE
IVDW   = 12
LREAL  = .FALSE.     # real-space projection off for accurate forces
NELM   = 120
# In POSCAR selective dynamics: T T T only for molecule atoms, F F F for all Au.
#
# Raman intensities are not native in VASP: use the vasp_raman.py finite-field
# approach (loop over modes, compute polarizability via LEPSILON/LCALCEPS), or
# use Quantum ESPRESSO ph.x for a slab (heavier). IR intensities: LEPSILON=.TRUE.
# Compare the L vs D adsorbed spectra -> the predicted SERS chirality difference.
